WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.059 --> 00:00:09.521
Hello, I'm Maria Rigatoni.

2
00:00:10.361 --> 00:00:12.722
Welcome to Italy, and welcome to my house.

3
00:00:13.663 --> 00:00:16.805
In Italy there is so much to see and so much to do.

4
00:00:17.665 --> 00:00:20.167
But best of all, there is so much to eat.

5
00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:25.029
Italy is famous for pizza, pasta, and the world's best ice cream.

6
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.332
Today I will be making spaghetti with tomato sauce for lunch.

7
00:00:31.228 --> 00:00:34.371
The first thing we need to do is to make a nice pile of flour.

8
00:00:35.332 --> 00:00:38.034
Then we make a big hole in the top of our pile.

9
00:00:38.894 --> 00:00:39.695
Just like this.

10
00:00:40.396 --> 00:00:41.316
It's for the eggs.

11
00:00:42.277 --> 00:00:45.100
Now carefully we crack four eggs into the hole.

12
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.382
Add just a little bit of water, not too much.

13
00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:51.485
Next we mix all the ingredients together.

14
00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:55.108
Now you have to knead the dough.

15
00:00:55.928 --> 00:00:56.969
This is the hard part.

16
00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:01.264
You have to push and fold, push and fold, push and fold.

17
00:01:01.964 --> 00:01:02.705
Keep kneading!

18
00:01:03.305 --> 00:01:04.625
It makes your hands sore.

19
00:01:05.525 --> 00:01:08.926
Now the dough is perfect, but it has to sit for thirty minutes.

20
00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.567
While we wait, I'll tell you a story.

21
00:01:12.607 --> 00:01:16.889
In the thirteenth century, there was an Italian man named Marco Polo.

22
00:01:18.409 --> 00:01:21.210
He was a great explorer and a famous Italian.

23
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:28.672
When Marco was only 14 years old, his father decided to go on a voyage of exploration.

24
00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:34.492
Marco begged his father to take him along, and finally his father agreed.

25
00:01:35.432 --> 00:01:38.775
They traveled all the way to China and they had great adventures.

26
00:01:41.036 --> 00:01:47.781
During their voyage, Marco saw many things that Italians had never seen before, such as eyeglasses and ice

27
00:01:47.821 --> 00:01:51.944
cream. But best of all, he discovered long, thin noodles.

28
00:01:52.725 --> 00:01:56.788
Marco Polo brought these noodles to Italy, and we called them spaghetti.

29
00:01:58.544 --> 00:02:05.469
Some historians claim that Marco Polo discovered noodles in the Arab world, and historians still debate whether he

30
00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.231
really discovered them in China.

31
00:02:07.991 --> 00:02:15.397
Nonetheless, it is widely accepted by the Italians that spaghetti noodles were first imported to Italy from China.

32
00:02:16.958 --> 00:02:19.260
Okay, we are ready for the next step.

33
00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.462
This is my pasta maker.

34
00:02:22.182 --> 00:02:24.204
Today I'll use it to make spaghetti noodles.

35
00:02:25.052 --> 00:02:27.674
We take our dough and put it in the pasta maker.

36
00:02:28.374 --> 00:02:29.415
Then presto!

37
00:02:29.895 --> 00:02:32.136
We have long, thin lines of spaghetti.

38
00:02:33.977 --> 00:02:35.919
Next we have to boil the spaghetti.

39
00:02:36.619 --> 00:02:39.861
We take our noodles and carefully put them into boiling water.

40
00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:45.064
Now we have to wait for ten minutes, so I will tell you another story.

41
00:02:45.844 --> 00:02:47.505
Do you see this tomato sauce?

42
00:02:48.226 --> 00:02:51.468
When we serve this on top of spaghetti, it tastes delicious.

43
00:02:53.600 --> 00:03:01.402
We make this sauce by boiling tomatoes, other vegetables, and spices for many, many hours―sometimes as long as

44
00:03:01.582 --> 00:03:02.023
one day.

45
00:03:02.683 --> 00:03:06.204
But did you know that at one time we didn't have tomatoes in Italy?

46
00:03:06.904 --> 00:03:08.885
Tomatoes had to come from Mexico.

47
00:03:10.905 --> 00:03:15.847
In the sixteenth century, the people who explored Mexico found fresh tomatoes.

48
00:03:16.687 --> 00:03:20.428
Because they were so delicious, they decided to bring some back to Europe.

49
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.901
Soon we began to grow tomatoes in Italy.

50
00:03:26.203 --> 00:03:30.605
Because of the warm sun and good soil, tomatoes grew very well in Italy.

51
00:03:31.325 --> 00:03:34.367
So we began making many kinds of foods from tomatoes.

52
00:03:35.087 --> 00:03:38.149
Tomato sauce is now the most famous Italian sauce.

53
00:03:38.929 --> 00:03:41.110
It is used for spaghetti and pizza.

54
00:03:43.632 --> 00:03:45.593
Ah, the spaghetti is ready.

55
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:49.035
Now we pour the hot noodles into the strainer.

56
00:03:49.815 --> 00:03:51.156
Then we put them on a plate.

57
00:03:52.013 --> 00:03:53.897
Last, we add some tomato sauce.

58
00:03:54.879 --> 00:03:56.724
And here you are, Mrs.

59
00:03:56.844 --> 00:03:58.067
Rigatoni's spaghetti.
